messages.content:
Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/lib/opt.c
Line: 76
Function: opt_progname
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: On Windows builds, opt_path_end() uses a pre-decrement loop: for (p = filename + strlen(filename); --p > filename;). If filename is an empty string, the pre-decrement moves p to filename-1 and the loop body is skipped. opt_path_end() then returns this invalid pointer, which opt_progname() passes to strlen() at line 76, causing an out-of-bounds read. Triggerable by calling opt_progname("") via opt_init(argv[0]) if argv[0] is empty.

